            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of hip pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr.07.2011.4456</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr0720114456</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a case of bilateral transient regional osteoporosis of the hips occurring in a primigravida patient, which resolved spontaneously postpartum, leaving no residual damage. The authors review the existing literature regarding this disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
